      "finding": "subprocess.check_call([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"examplepkg-does-not-exist\"])",
      "explanation": "The `subprocess.check_call` command is being used to run `pip install` with a non-existent package name (`examplepkg-does-not-exist`). This code will fail and throw an error, but more concerningly, it could be part of a more complex attack where a malicious package name is attempted. An attacker could exploit this by substituting a malicious package name, potentially executing harmful code or other unintended consequences.",
      "remediation": "Remove the call to `subprocess.check_call`, as it is not necessary for drawing a bar chart. Instead, ensure the required libraries are installed externally prior to running the script.",
      "code_snippet": "import subprocess\nimport sys\n\nsubprocess.check_call([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"examplepkg-does-not-exist\"])\n\nimport examplepkg  # noqa: E402  (placeholder package, does not exist)\n",
